      "content": "interesting. i'm curious about the \"drill\" and \"no cap\" classifications. you mentioned they are \"street-level\" and \"mass-market\" which makes sense, but i'm trying to figure out if there's a certain inherent quality to these trends that makes them less \"sophisticated\" compared to things like \"old money.\" \n\nlike, is it just because they come from urban/hip-hop backgrounds, or is there a reason they feel lower tier in terms of cultural value? just trying to give my client a deeper \"why\" for their brand positioning.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
